{
  "id": "cultural-blindness",
  "term": "cultural blindness",
  "definition": "Cultural blindness is an approach that treats culture as if it does not meaningfully affect people’s experiences or care. It is grounded in ideas of supposed universal applicability and assumptions about what is normal, which can make missing representation across race, sexual orientation, and social determinants of health seem acceptable and may reinforce this perspective.",
